Alembic migration directory.

Production databases use independent migration heads. The existing revisions
remain a shared compatibility history; all new revisions belong under the
matching `versions/core` or `versions/scenic` directory.

Upgrade both data domains explicitly:

    MYREID_MIGRATION_SCOPE=core alembic -c alembic.ini upgrade core@head
    MYREID_MIGRATION_SCOPE=scenic alembic -c alembic.scenic.ini upgrade scenic@head

Rollback the current revision for each data domain explicitly:

    MYREID_MIGRATION_SCOPE=core alembic -c alembic.ini downgrade -1
    MYREID_MIGRATION_SCOPE=scenic alembic -c alembic.scenic.ini downgrade -1

SQLite remains a local development fallback. It also runs the checked-in
Alembic revisions and no longer relies on SQLAlchemy `create_all()` or
startup-time `ALTER TABLE` repair code.

Run CLI commands from FastAPIBackend with the target DATABASE_URL and
SCENIC_DATABASE_URL exported, or inside the intended Compose container.
The CLI resolves its connection from the process environment / ini; copying
.env.prod alone does not load that file into the migration process.

As of 2026-10-15, the heads are 20261012100000_core and
20261012100000_scenic (media_files.size_bytes BIGINT). Compare `current`
with `heads` using each configuration before and after an upgrade.
The split audit checks revision suffixes, not equality with the latest head.

See docs/DATABASE_SPLIT_RUNBOOK.md and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md at repository root
for backup formats, recovery prerequisites and historical-table handling.
